First boot: the theme registers itself, the image chooses the default

Argon's own first-boot script registers its theme entry and, in the same batch,
writes `luci.main.mediaurlbase` — the design the web interface opens with. It does
that without asking what is already set, so in an image that ships Argon beside
another theme, Argon takes the default on every fresh install simply by being
installed. This removes that one line and leaves the registration: the theme stays
selectable at System -> Language and Style -> Design, an admin who chooses it keeps
it through a later upgrade, and the default is this image's own choice, written by
files/etc/uci-defaults/96-cw-default-theme after every package's script has run.
Nothing else about the package changes.

Applies to: https://github.com/jerrykuku/luci-theme-argon.git
            @ 7b77b44b8324ba4939144760ed3f09c1a1d1e833 (pinned in configs/local-packages.pin)
Applied by: tools/cw-release-build.sh, on the pinned commit before the package is
            installed, with `patch -p1 --fuzz=0` - the build fails if upstream
            changes these lines; re-port the patch then.
Upstream status: not submitted (a firmware's default theme is its own choice).

--- a/root/etc/uci-defaults/30_luci-theme-argon
+++ b/root/etc/uci-defaults/30_luci-theme-argon
@@ -63,7 +63,6 @@
 	uci get luci.themes.Argon >/dev/null 2>&1 || \
 	uci batch <<-EOF
 		set luci.themes.Argon=/luci-static/argon
-		set luci.main.mediaurlbase=/luci-static/argon
 		commit luci
 	EOF
 fi

